{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on ae6aeca9: accepted. R3b bounds `reusable` with one FIFO of at most 4,096 subject records, for every subject kind, as you propose. A new name at capacity drops the oldest entry. The bound adds no refusal and charges no signer key. Each input keeps its own records, and an in-flight input that holds a dropped record keeps that record.\n\nThe invariant in 22b57b9e changes. The sentence \"an act that names a real member gets the same outcome as on main\" is too strong, and this text replaces it:\n1. The map holds at most 4,096 records for any sequence of acts.\n2. A dropped entry only forces a fresh read. The scope never judges an act on an answer older than the answer main would use. After a drop, the act gets the outcome of the current Membership answer, or today's outcome for an unavailable read.\n3. One input sees one answer per subject from its start to its end.\n\nReason: the cached answer inside the 300-second window is an availability aid. A fresh answer is the more correct basis, so the difference that you name (removed member, unavailable read) is the safe direction. I accept the lost reuse.\n\nThree points for the implementation note:\n- State whether replay or `dap verify` reads this map. The entry records the observation that the act used, so my reading is that a drop cannot change a replay. Confirm or correct that from the source.\n- State the largest retained bytes of the map at 4,096 records: the count times the largest record that one subject can hold. If the product is above 16 MiB, stop and report before source edits. The bound then needs a byte limit too.\n- Record your reachability finding: an act from a key without established standing reaches `Further.read` when standing is null or unavailable, and through native grant marks.\n\nTests, kept small: one witness and one control. The witness sends signed Native acts that name more than 4,096 distinct absent members and reads the real map size. It then sends an act that names a real member whose entry the flood dropped, and shows one fresh read and the member's outcome. The control restores unbounded insertion and the witness fails on the size. Add no other eviction test.\n\nDocs: the threat-model sentence states the 4,096 bound and the fresh-read rule.\n\nOrder is unchanged: source edits start from R3a's frozen head after R3a's review request.\n\nSubagents: 784d14f6 says that your session needs a direct user or repository instruction to start subagents. Hugh gave that direction on 7 November (\"builder should be kept busy and use multiple subagents to progress work\"), recorded in lanes direction 0d6d0fba and in each lanes act since. If your session does not accept a workroom record as that instruction, keep the lanes in one session and say so. I have told Hugh.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}